The Tempest BBS program is a full featured BBS program with alot of options
and features.  For starters you may have :

      40 Message Bases.
      40 File Bases.
      40 Questions for people to Vote on.
      40 Online Doors (Games or Utilities).
      40 Bulletin Text Files.

   o   A system Password to logon to the system.
   o   A New User Password to keep your bbs private.
   o   Logon Time Can be selected by the Users Security Level.
   o   Baud rates can determine who may Connect, or Upload or Download.
   o   Reserve the BBS for a special caller.
   o   New Users are screened & given a series of questions they must answer.
   o   The Remote Sysop can Drop to Dos.  (ArpShell must be used)
   o   The Remote Sysop can edit other accounts or your own account while
       online.
   o   Online Editing of Accounts.
   o   With the Extra Setup Program the BBS can be edited from the background.
   o   Full featured doors are available.
   o   The Text Editor allows for Including the Message your replying to.
   o   And the Text Editor can also be used as a standard Text Editor for
       editing files to the BBS.
   o   A Logoff batch file, so the sysop may run tools to keep the BBS
       customized to his needs.
   o   There are also Codes you can place in text files to have information
       pop up.  Such as the users stats or information about the BBS.
       you can also place control characters to disable the text
       to stop every 22 lines,  or to make it where the User can not
       CTRL-C to break out of important text files.
   o   There are seperate Byte & File Ratios, and how many Files & Bytes
       a user may download in one day.
   o   2 Color chat so you know who's been typing away.  With the option
       of hit CTRL-C to get a time bar so you know how long you have
       been online chatting.
   o   There is the option for Arc, Zoo, Lharc, Wrp   Verifing.
   o   An option to scan all new files in all 40 File Areas or doing
       a Locate for a file.
   o   The remote sysop can fully edit the Files that are available for
       downloading.
   o   There are 3 type of log files the BBS can keep.  A transcript of
       everything a user types & see's.  Or a Callers log of just the
       important BBS Stuff.  And the Debug Log which keeps track of
       all the errors you may when running the BBS such as missing
       text files.

Individaul User Stats:
   o   Number of times a user may call in a day.
   o   Number of Messages a User may send in one day.
   o   Set how much a person can download and how is ratio is defined.
   o   How long they can stay on the BBS.
   o   Plus security flags for the 40 Message & File Bases & The
       privleges given to any user.
   o   Plus a whole lot more...(TOO MANY TO LIST)

Some Features in the File Transfers:
  o    Useing the HST old 9600 I am able to get 1150-1200 cps or so on
       archived files.
  o    Trying the BBS with the 14.4 modems speeds were recorded at
       1650-1750 cps or so just depending on the method of archiving.
  o    There is Batch Downloading by either file names or by wildcards.
  o    There is Batch Uploading.
  o    There is Resume with either uploading or downloading.
  o    And a full status screen is being displayed to watch the transfer.
  o    If the user has the proper access he can then download directly
       from any directory.  By file name or by WildCards.
  o    There are 4 different modes of viewing files,
       Quick Scan (4 across), Single Line, Double Line, Verbose Display.
  o    When viewing files you can view Oldest uploaded first or Newest
       files first.
  o    Each File Area can be used for,
         (Uploading Only)  (Downloading Only) or (Uploading & Downloading)
  o    Plus a whole lot more!

Some Features of the Message Base:
  o    You may leave mail to any user.
  o    Send it Public or Privatly or Protect it with a Password.
  o    You may also send priority mail where users are forced to read it.
  o    You may send Anounymous messages.
  o    You can trace the Author.
  o    You can also List all the replies to that message so you can follow
       the thread.
  o    Reply to a message
  o    The abilty to EDIT a already written letter.
  o    Plus other features to make message reading & writing easier.

NOTE:
      The features are not written in stone,  but as of this writing
      1/10/91 they are all active and useable.  But I may remove a few or
      add others,  just depending on the response from the registered
      users.
      All transfers were done with Zmodem protocol.

There are other features but there are just too many to list and i'm
